onapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxffe6wkcvpoouonjwfvprn7kecx9uau1ilkxukwko9dywbuwgp4z-hkesvxgkujobfrowobzskcjtyhennrmz0nzjlhsursf0e4prdtvkumzaf3fg2tirre-bkv1gqox9ezzthqemg4c-t6pye3681dz-697e938f.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxffe6wkcvpoouonjwfvprn7kecx9uau1ilkxukwko9dywbuwgp4z-hkesvxgkujobfrowobzskcjtyhennrmz0nzjlhsursf0e4prdtvkumzaf3fg2tirre-bkv1gqox9ezzthqemg4c-t6pye3681dz-697e938f.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"With a new branch created, you’ll be given a new Postgres connection string, which can be helpful when testing changes made to your branch from within an application.\"}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L62\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxe4h1gajbuwlkncxddjcpjq6pomnlvk4ljwehvphom2ur8nacmyojqulhlpk7w0vo6oejxao4eb2jzbxecycxzlqrcj2iy6bxn0qbvbujven2jwb-bq0e3tcwjckfz2npnirfgnikkdllnani2vw8ctnui-bf70675b.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxe4h1gajbuwlkncxddjcpjq6pomnlvk4ljwehvphom2ur8nacmyojqulhlpk7w0vo6oejxao4eb2jzbxecycxzlqrcj2iy6bxn0qbvbujven2jwb-bq0e3tcwjckfz2npnirfgnikkdllnani2vw8ctnui-bf70675b.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n70:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To make schema changes on your branch, head over to the \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"SQL Editor\"}],\" to make schema changes to your development branch.\"]}]\n71:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L62\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxd3ssw6s8twsxvs2llppgpy3ngv73db5wpauqczxo5wdeygtatzgcgrbgyzpt1ko68hmckg5wbzqfz6ygbshxiwticy3b4p1ut2d7ooqtfvqtyrz16q2afbm8csjhncrlb20ceobpr0kray4g-do32z3m-5d535c3e.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxd3ssw6s8twsxvs2llppgpy3ngv73db5wpauqczxo5wdeygtatzgcgrbgyzpt1ko68hmckg5wbzqfz6ygbshxiwticy3b4p1ut2d7ooqtfvqtyrz16q2afbm8csjhncrlb20ceobpr0kray4g-do32z3m-5d535c3e.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n72:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Once you’ve made the relevant changes on your development branch, head back over to \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Branches\"}],\" and select your development branch.\"]}]\n73:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L62\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxfvziotc1xbiiamkyfe4rcqesumcmzvp5ywnsrc9cqwj8sofrzjpi7fuxz-sd4vzwkyt9ier-uconxswymwsa9zdkg0nf24qzbgna36mjyamq9jsrx0aanaxbezg-yoiqrbl8rsmxknazjgqkse6dq-27090230.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxfvziotc1xbiiamkyfe4rcqe"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"sumcmzvp5ywnsrc9cqwj8sofrzjpi7fuxz-sd4vzwkyt9ier-uconxswymwsa9zdkg0nf24qzbgna36mjyamq9jsrx0aanaxbezg-yoiqrbl8rsmxknazjgqkse6dq-27090230.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n74:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"On the next screen select \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Open schema diff\"}],\" to see the changes that have been made to your development branch and how they differ from the main branch.\"]}]\n75:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L62\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxew83xktkt9w8emivwilyhkcvuemgbzwkuwohp0insm22qwr5udc4rmio2hpyk3u2s8fbhvvstxm0yrwaks8issr6mbeqikhjtmreu99f7khg3jv6zvokbdueup2jqsn5nvudihghjwj-b03a2ogmtq-a925d69d.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxew83xktkt9w8emivwilyhkcvuemgbzwkuwohp0insm22qwr5udc4rmio2hpyk3u2s8fbhvvstxm0yrwaks8issr6mbeqikhjtmreu99f7khg3jv6zvokbdueup2jqsn5nvudihghjwj-b03a2ogmtq-a925d69d.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n76:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"On the Schema Diff page you’ll see the changes that have been made. In our case you can see that a new column named \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"flag\"}],\" has been added with a data type of \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"varying(255)\"}],\".\"]}]\n77:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L62\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxd347b26wprtyq14lfcrniouoga849trsp0xospsxu2hu05gnx4bwkf0za43c53i63pgv9c6ggpmicaawq1zsvzfhp0baudy8n553wxybenve4xinxbbjagubpvo2g7gxbhmbebyunoyiuke3nwkejczk-7ba83b7b.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/neon-twin-deploy-workflow/ad4nxd347b26wprtyq14lfcrniouoga849trsp0xospsxu2hu05gnx4bwkf0za43c53i63pgv9c6ggpmicaawq1zsvzfhp0baudy8n553wxybenve4xinxbbjagubpvo2g7gxbhmbebyunoyiuke3nwkejczk-7ba83b7b.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n78:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Now you’re documenting the changes that have been made to the development branch. You’re ready to proceed with migrating them back to your production database.\"}]\n79:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"tested-in-neon-to-deployed-in-rds-two-methodologies\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Tested in Neon to deployed in RDS: Two methodologies\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#tested-in-neon-to-deployed-in-rds-two-methodologies\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Tested in Neon to deployed in RDS: Two methodologies\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$64:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n7a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"When it comes to migrating changes from your Neon Twin back to your AWS RDS production database, there are a couple of efficient approaches you can adopt. Each method has its own strengths, depending on your specific workflow and preferences.\"}]\n7b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"In the following sections, we’ll explore these two methodologies:\"}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Using SQL Files and\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"psql\"}],\". This “traditional” approach gives you full control over the migration process. By manually crafting .sql files, you can define the precise changes needed in your production database. These SQL scripts are then applied using psql.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Using Prisma ORM.\"}],\" If you’re using \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.prisma.io\",\"children\":\"Prisma\"}],\", you have an alternative. Prisma’s migration tooling simplifies the management of database schemas, and you can use this to "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"generate migration scripts based on the changes you’ve migrated (or applied) to your production database.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n7d:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"method-1-using-psql-with-github-actions-to-run-migrations\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Method 1: Using psql with GitHub Actions to run migrations\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#method-1-using-psql-with-github-actions-to-run-migrations\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Method 1: Using psql with GitHub Actions to run migrations\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$64:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"For this example, we’ve prepared an example repository where migrations can be written in SQL and will be applied by a GitHub Action that runs when a branch is merged into main:\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"👉 Example repo:\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/neondatabase/neon-twin-sql-migrations\",\"children\":\"neon-twin-sql-migrations\"}]]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"PR #1: \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/neondatabase/neon-twin-sql-migrations/pull/1/files\",\"children\":\"https://github.com/neondatabase/neon-twin-sql-migrations/pull/1/files\"}]]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n81:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"manual-sql-migrations-github-action\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Manual SQL Migrations GitHub Action\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#manual-sql-migrations-github-action\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Manual SQL Migrations GitHub Action\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"htt